# Docs report — etude-n9b.2

Documentation now matches the implemented checkout-read contract.

ANCESTOR: `etude-n9b` (P1) delivers GitHub issue #16 while preserving the
output-only default. MEASUREMENT: the feature changes what evidence a live gate
seat is authorized to inspect, so the workflow switch, manifest audit field,
trusted enforcement boundary, and temporary GH #14 restriction must be visible
to workflow authors and run auditors.

BLAST RADIUS: none: worktree and repo only.

## Updated

- `docs/run.md` documents `gate.read_checkout: true`, the output-only default,
  gate-wide model-seat scope, checks-only false resolution, the dedicated
  detached checkout, supervised-gate rejection, strict-reader compatibility,
  manifest audit semantics, and the fail-closed gitlink boundary.
- `docs/gates.md` documents that all live model seats now receive one shared
  policy-bearing prompt, the exact authoritative-provenance/no-rederived-
  arithmetic/falsification/BLOCK rule, the trusted prompt/harness boundary,
  the dedicated pin, and `GateAttempt.read_checkout` semantics.

The docs explicitly avoid claiming OS-level sandboxing. Read-only behavior is a
policy for trusted configured seat harnesses; the dedicated checkout prevents
stage and deterministic-check mutations from changing the seat's pinned code.

## Checked, no change

- `docs/replay.md`: stage replay behavior is unchanged. Forward replay reuses
  the documented live gate path and recorded SHA, so duplicating the gate
  access contract in the stage-replay guide would be misleading.
- CLI reference: no CLI command or flag changed.

## Known limitation

GitHub issue #14 is still open. The docs say opted-in reads fail closed on an
actual submodule gitlink; they do not present submodule reads as shipped support.
